.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH procquarium 1  "procquarium 0.4.0" 
.SH NAME
procquarium \- Your running processes, as fish.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBprocquarium\fR [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-fish\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\fR] [\fB\-\-kernel\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-\-screensaver\fR] [\fB\-\-feed\fR] [\fB\-\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-record\fR] [\fB\-\-replay\fR] [\fB\-\-kill\fR] [\fB\-\-colors\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
A terminal aquarium where every fish is a process on your machine. Big fish use a lot of memory, fast fish are burning CPU, and when a process exits its fish quietly floats to the surface. Leave it running in a spare pane, or use it as a screensaver.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<SECS>\fR
Seconds between process samples
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-fish\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum number of fish in the tank
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
Only show processes owned by this user
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\fR \fI<REGEX>\fR
Only show processes whose name matches this regex
.TP
\fB\-\-kernel\fR
Include kernel threads
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use plain ASCII glyphs instead of the Unicode ones
.TP
\fB\-\-screensaver\fR
Exit on any key or mouse event; hide labels and the info box
.TP
\fB\-\-feed\fR
Let `f` drop food; fish that eat get a small priority nudge (needs privileges to raise priority, and only ever touches your own processes)
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fI<N>\fR
Fixed random seed, for a reproducible tank
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a TOML config file (theme and defaults)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Don\*(Aqt capture the mouse, so text selection keeps working
.TP
\fB\-\-record\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write every snapshot as a JSON line to this file
.TP
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Replay snapshots from a recording instead of sampling
.TP
\fB\-\-kill\fR
Allow `k` to send SIGTERM to the selected process (asks first)
.TP
\fB\-\-colors\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Colour handling: auto (default), truecolor, 256 or none
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Truecolour when the terminal advertises it, else 256\-colour
.IP \(bu 2
truecolor: Always 24\-bit RGB
.IP \(bu 2
256: Always the nearest of the 256 xterm colours
.IP \(bu 2
none: No colour, the same as setting `NO_COLOR`
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  procquarium                      open the tank
  procquarium \-\-screensaver        any key or mouse event exits
  procquarium \-\-user $USER         only your own processes
  procquarium \-\-max\-fish 120       a crowded tank
  procquarium \-\-filter \*(Aq^rust\*(Aq \-\-interval 0.5
  procquarium \-\-feed               drop food with f
  procquarium \-\-seed 7             the same tank every time
  procquarium \-\-config tank.toml   your own colours, sprites and defaults
  procquarium \-\-record run.jsonl   save a session
  procquarium \-\-replay run.jsonl   play it back later

Keys while running:
  q / Esc          quit
  Space            pause the tank
  l                show or hide process names
  Tab / Shift+Tab  cycle fish and show details (PID, CPU, memory)
  + / \-            more or fewer fish
  f                drop food (with \-\-feed)
  /                search for a process by name
  k                send SIGTERM to the selected process (with \-\-kill)
  click a fish     select it (click empty water to clear)
.SH VERSION
v0.4.0
